o describe the moon's illuminated and darkened portions in the schematic style of the Astronomical Book rather than in modern scientific terms.", "reason": "cultural_note"}, {"marker": "c", "text": "Or 'seven parts of one, and all its disk is empty of light except for seven parts of it—fourteen parts of its light.'.", "reason": "previous_rendering"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 73:6", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "ወበዕለተ፡ ትነሥእ፡ ሳብዐተ፡ እደ፡ መንፈቀ፡ ብርሃኑ፡ ወይከውን፡ ብርሃኑ፡ ሳብዐተ፡ እደ፡ አሐተ፡ ወመንፈቃ።", "language": "Geez", "validation": "current_yaml_comparison", "chapter_file": "sources/enoch/ethiopic/transcribed/charles_1906/ch73.txt", "pages": [175, 176]}, "current_canonical_source_text": "ወበዕለተ፡ ትነሥእ፡ ሳብዐተ፡ እደ፡ መንፈቀ፡ ብርሃኑ፡ ወይከውን፡ ብርሃኑ፡ ሳብዐተ፡ እደ፡ አሐተ፡ ወመንፈቃ።", "translation": {"text": "And on the day it takes up a seventh part of half of its light[c][b][a], and its light becomes one and a half seventh parts.", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "The underlying expression is literally 'seven hands,' an idiom for measured portions or units in this astronomical context.", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "The final numbers are difficult in English. The Ge'ez reads literally along the lines of 'seven parts, one and a half,' so the verse likely describes a fractional increase in the moon's light.", "reason": "textual_variant"}, {"marker": "c", "text": "Or 'she rises, she takes seven parts from half of her light, and her light becomes seven parts and one half'.", "reason": "previous_rendering"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 73:7", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "ወየዓርብ፡ ምስለ፡ ፀሐይ፡ ወሶበ፡ ይሠርቅ፡ ፀሐይ፡ ይሠርቅ፡ ወርኅ፡ ምስሌሁ፡ ወይነሥእ፡ መንፈቀ፡ እደ፡ ብርሃን፡ ወበይእቲ፡ ሌሊት፡ በ*ርእሰ፡ ጽባሐ፡ ዚአሁ፡ በቅድመ፡ ዕለቱ፡ ለወርኅ፡ የዓርብ፡ ወርኅ፡ ምስለ፡ ፀሐይ፡ ወይጸልም፡ በይእቲ፡ ሌሊት፡ ፯ሳብዓተ፡ እደ፡ ወንፍቃ።", "language": "Geez", "validation": "current_yaml_comparison", "chapter_file": "sources/enoch/ethiopic/transcribed/charles_1906/ch73.txt", "pages": [175, 176]}, "current_canonical_source_text": "ወየዓርብ፡ ምስለ፡ ፀሐይ፡ ወሶበ፡ ይሠርቅ፡ ፀሐይ፡ ይሠርቅ፡ ወርኅ፡ ምስሌሁ፡ ወይነሥእ፡ መንፈቀ፡ እደ፡ ብርሃን፡ ወበይእቲ፡ ሌሊት፡ በ*ርእሰ፡ ጽባሐ፡ ዚአሁ፡ በቅድመ፡ ዕለቱ፡ ለወርኅ፡ የዓርብ፡ ወርኅ፡ ምስለ፡ ፀሐይ፡ ወይጸልም፡ በይእቲ፡ ሌሊት፡ ፯ሳብዓተ፡ እደ፡ ወንፍቃ።", "translation": {"text": "And it sets with the sun[a]; and when the sun rises, the moon rises with it and takes half a portion of light. And on that night, at the beginning of its morning, before the day[c][b], the moon sets with the sun and is dark through that night—seven parts and a half.", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "The Ge'ez wording is difficult in the middle of the verse, especially around 'at the beginning of its morning, before the day.' The translation keeps the temporal sequence fairly literal rather than smoothing it into a modern astronomical explanation.", "reason": "textual_variant"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "The chapter repeatedly measures lunar light in numbered 'parts.' The phrase rendered 'half a portion of light' likely refers to that same system of fractional illumination.", "reason": "cultural_note"}, {"marker": "c", "text": "Or 'before the day, the moon sets'.", "reason": "previous_rendering"}]}}, {"reference": "1 Enoch 73:8", "source": {"edition": "charles-1906-enoch", "text": "ወይሠርቅ፡ በይእቲ፡ ዕለት፡ ሳብዐተ፡ እደ፡ ጥንቁቀ፡ ወይወፅእ፡ ወይፀንእ፡ እምሥራቀ፡ ፀሐይ፡ ወ*ያበርህ፡ በትርፈ፡ ዕለቱ፡ *ስድስተ፡ ወሰብዓተ፡ እደ።", "language": "Geez", "validation": "unapplied_whole_printed_unit_candidate", "chapter_file": "sources/enoch/ethiopic/transcribed/charles_1906/ch73.txt + sources/enoch/ethiopic/transcribed/charles_1906/ch74.txt", "pages": [175, 176, 177]}, "current_canonical_source_text": "ወይሠርቅ፡ በይእቲ፡ ዕለት፡ ሳብዐተ፡ እደ፡ ጥንቁቀ፡ ወይወፅእ፡", "translation": {"text": "And on that day it rises with exactly seven parts[b][a], and it comes out.", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "The underlying phrase may also be rendered 'through that eastern gate/portal.' The Ge'ez OCR is somewhat uncertain at this point, but the sense is of a specific horizon-opening used in the luminary's course.", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "Or 'And on that seventh day he turns back by that eastern opening, and he goes out.'.", "reason": "previous_rendering"}]}}]
